From: danchapman <dantchapman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kk: sparse residency from a texture without ShaderWrite

Claude discovered a bug in Apple's Metal on M3. For sparse textures created with "shader write" permission,
Metal reports wrongly which parts of the texture have memory behind them.
This was confirmed with a small standalone Metal program.
The patch gives each affected texture a read-only twin that shares the same memory,
and the driver checks the twin instead.
Seen on macOS 26.6, M3 Max.

Generated-by: LLM

